From 90785df0d7a2d7a06bd0c94aa3f3aff045bec247 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 05:06:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: loads through openweb.fetch beside curl on the Amiga

ResourceHandleAmiga.cpp gets a second backend, picked at run time with
the Shell variable OB_NET: curl (the default) or openweb. The cookies,
redirects, the HTTP cache hook, file: URLs and synchronous loads stay
where they were and serve both; the curl delegate and the new backend
reach the handle through the same calls (amigaDidReceiveResponse with a
plain request, header lines and response, amigaDidReceiveData,
amigaDidFinish, amigaDidFail, amigaCancelRequest).

WebFetchAmiga.cpp is the request on the wire: one network thread opens
openweb.fetch (the card, a Cradle, or this Amiga's own TCP/IP and
OpenTLS) and moves every load on with asynchronous calls
(wf_async_start, wf_wait), waking on the network or on a signal from
the main thread. The request text comes from the ResourceRequest
(method, URL without its fragment, headers with the cookie jar's
Cookie, Accept-Language as curl added it); a body is read from FormData
(bytes, files, resolved blobs) and sent in 64 KB parts through wf_send,
CurlFormDataStream's job; the head becomes a ResourceResponse through
AmigaResponseHead; body parts go to the client as they come, after it
has taken the response. Credentials from the URL go in the request's
URL, for the transport's Basic or Digest answer to a 401, and only to
the URL's own server. Proxies are the transport's (its environment
variables). Errors are AmigaNetworkErrorDomain's. The card's host
decodes compressed bodies (WF_DECODE); the native transport has no
decoder until the datatypes' stream classes are there, so it asks for
"Accept-Encoding: identity".

OpenWebFetchAmiga.c holds the calls to openamigaservice's client in
plain C. It finds the client's headers when the browser's build gives
them; without them it builds empty, OB_NET=openweb is ignored and curl
loads.
